      "body": "@vidyuth-krishna yea please disclose all these information. Because I had been running DeepSeek v3.2 and GLM.51-FP8 with `vllm/vllm-openai-rocm:nightly` docker image without issue on mi300x. I would like to know what could be the condition that could contribute to this error.",
      "created_at": "2026-05-28T04:37:39Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/43804#issuecomment-4560867727",
      "id": 4560867727,
      "updated_at": "2026-05-28T04:37:57Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "tjtanaa"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Thanks for checking.\r\n\r\nThis issue was observed specifically from the AMD CI failure logs during the sparse attention ragged decode test path:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npytest tests/kernels/attention/test_rocm_triton_attn_dsv4.py::test_sparse_attn_decode_ragged_kernel -v\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe failing kernel path was in:\r\n`vllm/v1/attention/ops/rocm_aiter_mla_sparse.py`\r\n\r\nwith the Triton compile error:\r\n\r\n```text\r\ntype fp8e4b15 not supported in this architecture\r\nsupported fp8 dtypes are:\r\n('fp8e4b8', 'fp8e4nv', 'fp8e5', 'fp8e5b16')\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis was observed on gfx942/MI300 in ROCm CI. I do not currently have local MI300 hardware access, so I could not reproduce it outside CI.\r\n\r\nBased on the logs, this appears to be isolated to the sparse/ragged decode kernel path rather than general FP8 inference workloads such as DeepSeek/GLM serving on the nightly ROCm image.\r\n\r\nRelevant CI log:\r\nhttps://buildkite.com/vllm/amd-ci/builds/8807/list?jid=019e6383-4ab7-4124-9f8d-5f24132dd3b4&tab=output\r\n",
      "created_at": "2026-05-28T19:52:04Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/43804#issuecomment-4567669458",
      "id": 4567669458,
      "updated_at": "2026-05-28T19:54:19Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "vidyuth-krishna"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "I think that DS4 should not be executed on MI300 and is only good for MI355 (gfx950 in general) but @tjtanaa can further confirm this (I am not sure). If that is true then this test should just be skipped on MI300.",
      "created_at": "2026-05-28T21:49:20Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/43804#issuecomment-4568626853",
      "id": 4568626853,
      "updated_at": "2026-05-28T21:49:20Z",
