    },
    {
      "body": "Quick update: I now have access to an MI300 (gfx942) system and was able to reproduce the issue locally.\r\n\r\nRunning:\r\n\r\n`pytest tests/kernels/attention/test_rocm_triton_attn_dsv4.py::test_sparse_attn_decode_ragged_kernel -v`\r\n\r\nfails with:\r\n\r\n```\r\ntype fp8e4b15 not supported in this architecture.\r\nThe supported fp8 dtypes are ('fp8e4b8', 'fp8e4nv', 'fp8e5', 'fp8e5b16')\r\n```\r\n\r\nI also tested replacing `tl.float8e4b15` with `tl.float8e4nv`.\r\n\r\nThat allows the kernel to compile and execute, but the test then fails numerical validation (~61% mismatched elements), indicating that fp8e4nv is not a correct drop-in replacement.\r\n\r\nGiven this, I'm wondering whether the DS4/FNUZ path is expected to run on gfx942 at all, or whether this test should be gated/skipped on MI300",
